# Plutus frontend configuration.
#
# Copy to .env only if you need to override a default. Local development normally
# needs none of this: leaving REACT_APP_API_URL unset keeps requests relative so the
# CRA dev server proxy (the "proxy" field in package.json) forwards them to the local
# backend.
#
# Two things to know about REACT_APP_* variables:
#   1. They are inlined at BUILD time, not read at runtime. Changing one in Vercel
#      requires a redeploy.
#   2. They end up in the JavaScript bundle that ships to the browser, so nothing
#      here is secret.

# Origin of the deployed API, with no trailing slash. Unset in development; set in
# Vercel to the production API, for example https://api.plutus.lakshayverma.com
# REACT_APP_API_URL=

# Demo credentials pre-filled on the sign-in form. Set these in Vercel only, so the
# public demo lets a visitor sign in with one click while local development keeps an
# empty form. The sign-in page shows a demo banner only when both are present.
# REACT_APP_DEMO_EMAIL=
# REACT_APP_DEMO_PASSWORD=
